-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/ad8fe5cc-57a7-51ec-affe-f8416dffa500
-- title:
--   Joint two-level semistable specialisation with widths and arithmetic Frobenius
-- statement:
--   Setting and hypotheses. Let $M$, $s$, $q'$ be non-zero natural numbers, with $s$ prime (`hs`), $q'$ prime (`hq'`), $s \neq q'$ (`hsq'`), $q' \nmid M$ (`hq'M`) and $s \nmid M$ (`hsM`). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q'`, that is, the image of $q'$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $k := \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, which then has characteristic $q'$ (via [`ValuationSubring.charP_residueField_of_liesOverPrime_def`](def/WeierstrassCurve_ReductionMap.html#L57)). The two sets `ssPlaces q' (M*s) k` and `ssPlaces q' M k` — the places of `modularFunctionFieldC k (M*s)`, resp. `modularFunctionFieldC k M` (the subfield of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by $j(q)$ and $j(q^{N})$ for the respective level $N$) satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace` — are assumed finite. Throughout, `JZero N` denotes $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, carrying the Hecke-module structure `heckeModuleBar N` for the four levels $(Ms)q'$, $Ms$, $Mq'$ and $M$; `HeckeAlg` is $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ with `heckeGen ℓ` $= X_\ell$; `inertiaInvariants A N` is the subgroup of `JZero N` fixed by `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$); `PrimeToTorsion q' x` says that $n \cdot x = 0$ for some $n > 0$ with $q' \nmid n$; and `toricMonodromyPart q' I` is the `HeckeAlg`-submodule spanned by the elements $\sigma \cdot x - x$ with $\sigma \in I$ and $x$ killed by some positive integer coprime to $q'$.
--
--   Existential data. The assertion is that there exist: `HeckeAlg`-module structures on $\mathrm{Pic}^0_k(\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ (M s))$ and on $\mathrm{Pic}^0_k(\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ M)$ (two anonymous witnesses, not further constrained); semistable specialisation data $D_1$ of type `JZeroSemistableSpecialization A (M*s) q' hq'` and $D_2$ of type `JZeroSemistableSpecialization A M q' hq'` — each such datum consists of a finite set `nodes` of pairs of places of the corresponding characteristic-$q'$ modular function field whose residue fields are generated by $k$, a semilinear automorphism `frob` whose base automorphism is $a \mapsto a^{q'}$, stabilising `nodes` and inducing an involution of the nodes, a width function `width : nodes → ℕ`, a component map `comp` from `inertiaInvariants A (N * q')` to `componentGroup width` (the $\mathbb{Z}$-dual of the character lattice modulo the image of the Gram map of the widths), a specialisation map `sp` from `inertiaInvariants A (N * q')` to the glued Picard group `GluedPic0 k (modularFunctionFieldC k N) nodes` (admissible pairs of degree-zero divisors vanishing at the node places, together with a node unit function into $\mathrm{Additive}\,k^{\times}$, modulo glued-principal data), a map `spN` from `JZero N` to $\mathrm{Pic}^0_k$ of the characteristic-$q'$ curve, and the compatibility axioms of the structure for `comp` and `sp` under Hecke operators and Frobenius; maps $ab : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to (\mathtt{ssPlaces}\,q'\,(Ms)\,k \to \mathtt{ssPlaces}\,q'\,M\,k)$; bijections $e_1$ from `ssPlaces q' (M*s) k` to $D_1$.nodes and $e_2$ from `ssPlaces q' M k` to $D_2$.nodes; weight functions $w$ on `ssPlaces q' (M*s) k` and $wV$ on `ssPlaces q' M k` with values in $\mathbb{N}_{>0}$; multiplicities $m : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathtt{ssPlaces}\,q'\,(Ms)\,k \to \mathbb{N}$; a pair of homomorphisms $\mathrm{dpair}\ i : \mathtt{JZero}\,((Ms)q') \to \mathtt{JZero}\,(Mq')$; and a pair of homomorphisms $\Phi\ i$ from `GluedPic0 k (modularFunctionFieldC k (M*s)) D₁.nodes` to `GluedPic0 k (modularFunctionFieldC k M) D₂.nodes`, such that the following conjuncts hold.
--
--   (1) $D_1.\mathrm{nodes} = \mathtt{nodePairsOfPlaces}\ D_1.\mathrm{frob}\ (\mathtt{ssPlaces}\,q'\,(Ms)\,k).\mathrm{toFinset}$, i.e. the node set is the image of the supersingular places under $w \mapsto (w, D_1.\mathrm{frob} \cdot w)$. (2) The same for $D_2$ with `ssPlaces q' M k`.
--
--   (3) For every supersingular place $p$ at level $Ms$, the first component of the node pair $e_1(p)$ is $p$. (4) The same for $e_2$ at level $M$.
--
--   (5) For every $\sigma$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` and every $x \in \mathtt{JZero}((Ms)q')$ with `PrimeToTorsion q' x`: $\sigma \cdot x - x$ lies in `inertiaInvariants A ((M*s)*q')`, and for that membership $D_1.\mathrm{comp}(\sigma \cdot x - x) = 0$ and `toPic0Pair` of $D_1.\mathrm{sp}(\sigma \cdot x - x)$ vanishes. (6) The same statement for $D_2$ and $x \in \mathtt{JZero}(Mq')$.
--
--   (7) For each $i$, $\mathrm{dpair}\ i$ carries `toricMonodromyPart q' (A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ)` of $\mathtt{JZero}((Ms)q')$ into `toricMonodromyPart q' (A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ)` of $\mathtt{JZero}(Mq')$.
--
--   (8) For each $i$, each inertia-invariant $x$ at level $(Ms)q'$ with $\mathrm{dpair}\ i\ x$ inertia-invariant at level $Mq'$, if $D_1.\mathrm{comp}\,x = 0$ then $D_2.\mathrm{sp}(\mathrm{dpair}\ i\ x) = \Phi\ i\ (D_1.\mathrm{sp}\,x)$.
--
--   (9) For each $i$ and each supersingular place $p$ at level $Ms$: $m\ i\ p \cdot w(p) = wV(ab\ i\ p)$. (10) For each $i$ and each supersingular place $v$ at level $M$: $\sum_{p \,:\, ab\ i\ p = v} m\ i\ p = s + 1$.
--
--   (11) For each $i$ and each node-unit function $g : D_1.\mathrm{nodes} \to \mathrm{Additive}\,k^{\times}$, $\Phi\ i\ (\mathtt{nodeUnit}\ D_1.\mathrm{nodes}\ g) = \mathtt{nodeUnit}\ D_2.\mathrm{nodes}\ \bigl(n_2 \mapsto \sum_{p_1 \,:\, ab\ i\ p_1 = e_2^{-1}(n_2)} m\ i\ p_1 \cdot g(e_1 p_1)\bigr)$.
--
--   (12) For each $i$, and for $y \in \mathtt{JZero}((Ms)q')$, $z \in \mathtt{JZero}((Mq')s)$ corresponding under the transport along $(Ms)q' = (Mq')s$ given by `Nat.mul_right_comm M s q'`: $\mathrm{dpair}\ i\ y = \mathtt{degeneracyPushforwardPair}\ (Mq')\ s\ i\ z$, the $i$-th of the two degeneracy pushforwards for level $Mq'$ and prime $s$ (the pushforwards along `heckeAlphaBar` and `heckeBetaBar` when the required inputs hold, and $0$ otherwise).
--
--   (13) $w(p) = D_1.\mathrm{width}(e_1 p)$ for every supersingular place $p$ at level $Ms$; (14) $wV(v) = D_2.\mathrm{width}(e_2 v)$ for every supersingular place $v$ at level $M$.
--
--   (15) A nine-clause package for $D_1$: (a) the inertia-displacement clause of (5), repeated verbatim; (b) for every $m$ coprime to $q'$, every $m$-torsion element $g$ of `GluedPic0 k (modularFunctionFieldC k (M*s)) D₁.nodes` is $D_1.\mathrm{sp}\,x$ for some inertia-invariant $x$ with $m \cdot x = 0$ and $D_1.\mathrm{comp}\,x = 0$; (c) for every $m$ coprime to $q'$, every $m$-torsion $\varphi \in \mathtt{componentGroup}\ D_1.\mathrm{width}$ equals $D_1.\mathrm{comp}\,x$ for some inertia-invariant $x$ with $m \cdot x = 0$; (d) $D_1.\mathrm{comp}$ is surjective; (e) for $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and inertia-invariant $x$ with $\sigma \cdot x$ again inertia-invariant, $D_1.\mathrm{comp}\,x = 0$ implies $D_1.\mathrm{comp}(\sigma \cdot x) = 0$; (f) in the same situation, if moreover `toPic0Pair` of $D_1.\mathrm{sp}\,x$ vanishes then so does `toPic0Pair` of $D_1.\mathrm{sp}(\sigma \cdot x)$; (g) in the same situation, if `toPic0Pair` of $D_1.\mathrm{sp}\,x$ equals $(D_1.\mathrm{spN}\,a, D_1.\mathrm{spN}\,b)$ for some $a, b \in \mathtt{JZero}(Ms)$, then `toPic0Pair` of $D_1.\mathrm{sp}(\sigma \cdot x)$ equals $(D_1.\mathrm{spN}(\sigma \cdot a), D_1.\mathrm{spN}(\sigma \cdot b))$; (h) all widths $D_1.\mathrm{width}$ are positive; (i) there is a `HeckeAlg`-module structure on $\mathtt{componentGroup}\ D_1.\mathrm{width}$ for which $D_1.\mathrm{comp}$ is equivariant, i.e. $D_1.\mathrm{comp}(T \cdot x) = T \cdot D_1.\mathrm{comp}\,x$ whenever both $x$ and $T \cdot x$ are inertia-invariant, and such that for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of `HeckeAlg` with $\mathtt{heckeTorsion}\,(\mathtt{componentGroup}\ D_1.\mathrm{width})\,\mathfrak{m} = \bot$, every $x$ in the $\mathfrak{m}$-torsion of $\mathtt{JZero}((Ms)q')$ which satisfies `PrimeToTorsion q' x`, is inertia-invariant, has $D_1.\mathrm{comp}\,x = 0$ and `toPic0Pair` of $D_1.\mathrm{sp}\,x$ zero, lies in `toricMonodromyPart q' (A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ)`.
--
--   (16) The same nine-clause package for $D_2$, with level $M$ in place of $Ms$ and $\mathtt{JZero}(Mq')$ in place of $\mathtt{JZero}((Ms)q')$.
--
--   (17) Hecke transport at level $Ms$: for every prime $\ell$ there are an integer matrix $T_\ell$ indexed by $D_1.\mathrm{nodes} \times D_1.\mathrm{nodes}$ and an integer $n_\ell$ such that $\sum_{t} T_\ell\,t\,s = n_\ell$ for every node $s$; and if $\ell \neq q'$ then $n_\ell$ is the degree $\mathtt{finrankAlong}\ k\ (\mathtt{heckeAlphaC}\ k\ (M s)\ \ell)$, and, assuming `HasPrincipalDivisors` for `charLDegeneracyRoof k (M*s) ℓ` and the integrality hypotheses `HeckeAlphaCIntegral` and `HeckeBetaCIntegral` at level $Ms$ and $\ell$, for all nodes $a, b$ the entry $T_\ell\,a\,b$ is the value at the first place of $a$ of the divisor correspondence (pullback along `heckeAlphaC` followed by pushforward along `heckeBetaC`) applied to the divisor $\mathtt{Finsupp.single}$ at the first place of $b$ with coefficient $1$; and, for every inertia-invariant $x$ at level $(Ms)q'$ with $\mathtt{heckeGen}\ \ell \cdot x$ again inertia-invariant and $D_1.\mathrm{comp}\,x = 0$, and every $w : D_1.\mathrm{nodes} \to \mathrm{Additive}\,k^{\times}$ with $D_1.\mathrm{sp}\,x = \mathtt{nodeUnit}\ D_1.\mathrm{nodes}\ w$, one has $D_1.\mathrm{sp}(\mathtt{heckeGen}\ \ell \cdot x) = \mathtt{nodeUnit}\ D_1.\mathrm{nodes}\ \bigl(t \mapsto \sum_{s} T_\ell\,s\,t \cdot w(s)\bigr)$. (18) The same clause at level $M$, for $D_2$ and $\mathtt{JZero}(Mq')$.
--
--   (19) Identification of $ab$ by restriction of places: for every pair $\varphi : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to (\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ M \to_{\mathrm{alg}} \mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ (Ms))$ of $k$-algebra maps with integral underlying ring maps, such that $\varphi\,0$ is the identity on Laurent series and $\varphi\,1$ is the $q \mapsto q^{s}$ substitution $\mathtt{qExpand}\ k\ s$, and for every $i$ and every supersingular place $p$ at level $Ms$: $\mathtt{Place.restrictAlong}\ (\varphi\ i)\ p = ab\ i\ p$.
--
--   (20) For each $i$, every inertia-invariant $x$ at level $(Ms)q'$ with $\mathrm{dpair}\ i\ x$ inertia-invariant at level $Mq'$ and $D_1.\mathrm{comp}\,x = 0$ satisfies $D_2.\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{dpair}\ i\ x) = 0$.
--
--   (21) $w(p) = \mathtt{placeWidthChar}\ q'\ (Ms)\ p$ for every supersingular place $p$ at level $Ms$, and (22) $wV(v) = \mathtt{placeWidthChar}\ q'\ M\ v$ for every supersingular place $v$ at level $M$, where `placeWidthChar q' N w` is $\mathtt{jWidthChar}\ q'$ of the value of $w$ at the generator $j$ of the $j$-line, divided by the ramification index `placeRamificationJ N w` of $w$ over the $j$-line.
--
--   (23) $D_1.\mathrm{frob} = \mathtt{arithFrobC}\ q'\ k\ (Ms)$ and (24) $D_2.\mathrm{frob} = \mathtt{arithFrobC}\ q'\ k\ M$, the semilinear automorphisms acting on coefficients by the $q'$-power Frobenius of $k$.
--
--   This is the geometric input, at a prime $q'$ of good reduction for the level $M$, to the level-lowering step: a pair of semistable specialisation data at levels $Ms$ and $M$ constructed together, so that the two degeneracy maps, the supersingular-place indexing, the node widths (in the characteristic-sensitive form valid also for $q' = 2, 3$) and the arithmetic Frobenius are simultaneously identified, and the component groups carry compatible Hecke actions. It is used by the canonical form of the two-level statement, [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_twoLevelSemistableSpecialization_jointConstruction_ssPlaces_heckeTransport_canonical_levelPrimeIntertwine_correspondence_arithFrobC_restrictAlong_placeWidthChar`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_twoLevelSemistableSpecialization_jointConstruction_ssPlaces_heckeTransport_canonical_levelPrimeIntertwine_correspondence_arithFrobC_restrictAlong_placeWidthChar).
